      "content": "When presenting arguments, focus on the immediate economic impact on local businesses. You could argue that the increased compliance costs will force smaller manufacturers to cut jobs or relocate to jurisdictions with less stringent regulations. Furthermore, point out that these sudden costs might reduce their competitiveness against international producers not facing the same burden, ultimately harming local economic stability. This framed argument centers on the practical, local consequences rather than the environmental goals of the regulations.",
      "source": "target",
