      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The proponents will emphasize that the regulations are a necessary step to mitigate long-term climate change impacts and protect public health. They will frame the standards not as a cost, but as an essential investment in a sustainable, future-proof economy. Their core argument is that inaction on emissions will lead to far greater economic and ecological damage down the line. By understanding this \"long-term necessity\" framing, you can better prepare counter-arguments about near-term economic pain.",
      "source": "target",
