      "content": "Your perspective touches upon a common friction point between broad policy goals and immediate local realities. Many economists argue that taxing local businesses for global issues creates an unfair disparity in risk and responsibility. You can argue that the burden of transition should be shared by large, multinational corporations who benefit most from global trade, rather than solely placed on local small and medium-sized enterprises. This frames the conflict as one of equitable burden distribution.",
      "source": "target",
